  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An ice skater extends his arms horizontally to the sides and as a result, his angular velocity about the vertical axis of rotation changes from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\omega}{3}\"></span>. The rotational kinetic energy of the ice skater before extending his arms to the sides is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span>. </p>\n<p>Given that no external torques act on the ice skater, what is the change in the rotational kinetic energy of the ice skater as a result of  extending his arms to the sides?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{E}{9}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{8E}{9}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{E}{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2E}{3}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
